10
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Zoey's Extraordinary Playlist is an American jukebox musical comedy-drama television
series created by Austin Winsberg that premiered on January 7, 2020, on NBC.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
The series stars Jane Levy as Zoey Clarke, a software developer who discovers she
has the ability to hear the innermost thoughts of people as songs.

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Each episode features multiple song-and-dance numbers that develop the
storyline, with each cast member singing their own character's songs.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
Except for the season 2 song "Crimson Love," the soundtrack
consists entirely of previously written popular songs.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
The series also stars Skylar Astin, Alex Newell, John Clarence Stewart, Peter Gallagher, Mary Steenburgen, Lauren
Graham, Andrew Leeds, Alice Lee, Michael Thomas Grant and Kapil Talwalkar, and Bernadette Peters.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
In June 2020, the series was renewed for a second
season which premiered on January 5, 2021.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
In June 2021, the series was canceled after two seasons.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
In 2021, streaming service The Roku Channel released
an original two-hour holiday film.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
In addition to songs performed on Zoey's Extraordinary Christmas, the second original song in the series — "North Star", written
by Mary Steenburgen, Caitlyn Smith and Troy Verges and sung by Tori Kelly — played during the end credit sequence.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of holiday, family, christmas.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
